Jev RAG Benchmark
=================

This project is an independent benchmark. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
by, or sponsored by TypeSafe AI, Codiv, Vercel, or NVIDIA. "Jev" is a model by
TypeSafe AI. Results published with this harness describe the exact model
versions recorded in each run manifest and must not be generalized to other
models.

Prior work
----------
The experimental design (hybrid candidate retrieval, frozen candidate pools,
reranker comparison, frozen-context answer generation, artifact manifests) was
inspired by the MIT-licensed project "jev-rag-benchmark" by erendikmenn
(https://github.com/erendikmenn/jev-rag-benchmark). No code was copied; this
harness was written from scratch and targets English datasets, calibration
analysis, and free-tier reproducibility.

Datasets
--------
- XQuAD (English): CC BY-SA 4.0. Artetxe et al., "On the Cross-lingual
  Transferability of Monolingual Representations" (2020).
  https://github.com/deepmind/xquad
- SciFact / BEIR: abstracts under ODC-By 1.0, annotations under CC BY 4.0.
  Wadden et al. (2020); Thakur et al., "BEIR" (2021).
  https://public.ukp.informatik.tu-darmstadt.de/thakur/BEIR/datasets/scifact.zip
Raw and processed datasets are downloaded at runtime and are not committed to
this repository.

Services
--------
- Vercel AI Gateway: TypeSafe-compatible endpoint used for the real Jev branch.
  https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway
- NVIDIA NIM (build.nvidia.com): free trial tier used for embeddings, the
  baseline cross-encoder, and (in earlier revisions) answer generation.
  Trial terms apply; this benchmark is research and testing use.
- Codiv: free public trial endpoint used for answer generation with
  DiffusionGemma 26B. https://codiv.ai/docs
